reviews.usertext:
The tour was very fun. Our guide - Godfrey, kept talking for most of the tour, which is definitely not a bad thing since he has a very good sense of humour.

About the objectives:
* Windsor castle is well worth the visit, the collection of weapons and armors is great, coupled with the art work it becomes a must;
* Bath looks like a beautiful town, only wish we would have had about 30 minutes more here. The Roman baths visit was quite informative;
* Stonehenge's history and tales are fascinating. The pastures and burial mounds around it make for a great landscape also

In conclusion, I highly recommend this tour.
